stion or hypothesis of FAM:SF-APPS-011 (0.79)"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "Regular season vs playoff PPP by play type (DRIVE over-prediction)", "auto_outcome_status": "supported", "observed_hypothesis": "DRIVE PPP is materially higher in RS than playoffs, so an RS-calibrated optimizer over-recommends DRIVE.", "observed_result": "DRIVE RS 1.198 vs PO 0.912 (-0.286, 25 teams); PNR -0.173; PULL_UP +0.301; others within -0.07.", "auto_failure_mechanism": "D_positive (no failure: positive result)", "observed_failure_evidence": "DRIVE playoff PPP 0.286 below RS across 25 teams; top-10 teams all -0.30 to -0.43.", "observed_sample_and_power": "25 teams, min 30 poss per cell; no CIs", "auto_validation_status": "no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED", "observed_method": "Team-level (team, PT, context) cells, min 30 poss, up to 25 teams.", "observed_verdict": "supported", "observed_failure_type": "D_positive", "observed_notes": "Motivated the playoff DRIVE exclusion and a proposed playoff DSI offset."}, "relationships": []}, {"id": "FAM:SF-CHT-052", "label": "Study family SF-CHT-052: Play-type replacement similarity vs absorb/cascade", "score": 0.857, "reached_via": ["request matches the question or hypothesis of FAM:SF-CHT-052 (0.75)"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "Play-type replacement similarity vs absorb/cascade", "auto_outcome_status": "inconclusive", "observed_hypothesis": "Having a similar-profile teammate separates absorption from cascade when a player sits.", "observed_result": "mean sim ABSORBED +0.863 vs CASCADE +0.848; Spearman(sim, -gap)=-0.19 (wrong-signed). Embiid 23-24 cascades with Reed sim 0.94.", "auto_failure_mechanism": "B_powered_null (adequately powered null result)", "observed_failure_evidence": "Similarity does not separate absorption from cascade; almost always findable.", "observed_sample_and_power": "NOT_RECORDED", "auto_validation_status": "no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED", "observed_verdict": "null", "observed_failure_type": "B_powered_null"}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_limited_by", "node": "LIM:label_or_classification_error"}, {"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:LABEL_ERROR"}, {"rel": "auto_related_family", "node": "FAM:SF-APPA-005"}, {"rel": "auto_related_family", "node": "FAM:SF-CHT-032"}, {"rel": "auto_related_family", "node": "FAM:SF-CHT-086"}]}, {"id": "FAM:SF-CHT-032", "label": "Study family SF-CHT-032: Teammate DRIVE then PNR including calibrated labels then inferrer-only", "score": 0.842, "reached_via": ["FAM:SF-CHT-052 auto_related_family (limitation_precedent) FAM:SF-CHT-032", "request matches RQC:RQC-039 (0.72); FAM:SF-CHT-032 auto_addresses_question RQC:RQC-039"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "Teammate DRIVE then PNR including calibrated labels then inferrer-only", "auto_outcome_status": "artifact", "observed_hypothesis": "Any teammate DRIVE preceding a PNR raises PNR PPP.", "observed_result": "League-wide including calibrated PNR: +0.022 PPP, p=0.004 (n=20,658 vs 159,623). Tatum +0.152 p=0.27. Inferrer-only DRIVE-PNR ATT=-0.006, p=0.76.", "auto_failure_mechanism": "C_artifact (apparent effect produced by a construction, selection or labelling flaw)", "observed_failure_evidence": "The +0.022 vanished to -0.006 once PNR was inferrer-only; calibrated-PNR temporal contamination.", "observed_sample_and_power": "n~180k including calibrated labels", "auto_validation_status": "no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED", "observed_verdict": "artifact_found", "observed_failure_type": "C_artifact"}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_limited_by", "node": "LIM:label_or_classification_error"}, {"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:LABEL_ERROR"}, {"rel": "auto_related_family", "node": "FAM:SF-APPA-005"}]}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPS-069", "label": "Study family SF-APPS-069: State persistence vs window-overlap null (pre-registered FAIL)", "score": 0.606, "reached_via": ["FAM:SF-APPS-073 auto_related_family (record_link_related_to) FAM:SF-APPS-069", "request matches DS:NBA_play_by_play_possessions_and_reconstructed_lineups (0.77); FAM:SF-APPS-069 auto_uses_dataset DS:NBA_play_by_play_possessions_and_reconstructed_lineups"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "State persistence vs window-overlap null (pre-registered FAIL)", "auto_outcome_status": "rejected", "observed_hypothesis": "Process-only latent state (PCA-1 of tempo/transition) persists above the rolling-window overlap null after game x team demeaning.", "observed_result": "Process-only lag-1 r=+0.645 vs null +0.655; EXCESS=-0.010, cluster-bootstrap 95% CI [-0.012,-0.009]. Scoring excess -0.000; action texture +0.003. Instantaneous scoring autocorr lag-1=-0.0128.", "auto_failure_mechanism": "B_powered_null (adequately powered null result)", "observed_failure_evidence": "HEADLINE FAIL: excess=-0.010 with CI entirely negative; state persistence does not clear the overlap null. No state-persistence paper.", "observed_sample_and_power": "N=1,060,893 possessions"}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_limited_by", "node": "LIM:small_sample"}, {"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:MECHANICAL_FLOOR"}, {"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER"}, {"rel": "auto_related_family", "node": "FAM:SF-APPS-059"}]}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPS-059", "label": "Study family SF-APPS-059: Sequence-memory horizon test (per-lag vs aggregated window)", "score": 0.501, "reached_via": ["FAM:SF-APPS-073 auto_related_family (record_link_related_to) FAM:SF-APPS-059", "request matches DS:NBA_play_by_play_possessions_and_reconstructed_lineups (0.77); FAM:SF-APPS-059 auto_uses_dataset DS:NBA_play_by_play_possessions_and_reconstructed_lineups"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "Sequence-memory horizon test (per-lag vs aggregated window)", "auto_outcome_status": "supported", "observed_hypothesis": "Increasing prior-possession history changes the opponent's next-possession outcome after controlling for game state.", "observed_result": "Per-lag GBT AUC N=0 0.5621 -> N=1 0.5863 (d+0.0242) -> N=3 0.5907 -> N=8 0.5911. R2 0.0051 -> 0.0133. Aggregated window declines after N=1 (AUC 0.5868 -> 0.5687 at N=8). Effective horizon ~2-3 possessions.", "auto_failure_mechanism": "D_positive (no failure: positive result)", "observed_failure_evidence": "Short-memory horizon is stable OOS; almost all gain is lag-1, plateau by lag 4. Absolute AUC still only ~0.591.", "observed_sample_and_power": "n=1,024,980 possessions; time-split test 2025-26", "observed_verdict": "supported"}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_limited_by", "node": "LIM:small_sample"}, {"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER"}, {"rel": "auto_related_family", "node": "FAM:SF-APPS-070"}, {"rel": "auto_related_family", "node": "FAM:SF17"}]}, {"id": "FAM:SF-CHT-037", "label": "Study family SF-CHT-037: Sequence-memory lag effects with game-state controls", "score": 0.482, "reached_via": ["FAM:SF-APPS-073 auto_related_family (limitation_precedent) FAM:SF-CHT-037", "request matches DS:Play_type_initiation_records_Neo4j_INITIATED_edges_play_type_possessions (0.73); FAM:SF-CHT-037 auto_uses_dataset DS:Play_type_initiation_records_Neo4j_INITIATED_edges_play_type_possessions"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "Sequence-memory lag effects with game-state controls", "auto_outcome_status": "artifact", "observed_hypothesis": "Naive lag-1 play-type PPP effects survive period/clock/margin controls and within-team baselines.", "observed_result": "Lag-1 real, lag-2 small, lag-3+ ~0: d(1)=+0.024 AUC, d(2)=+0.004. SPOT_UP lag-1 MWU_p=0.0000 with and without controls. DRIVE lag-1 MWU_p=0.0000 but ctrl_p=0.0911. PNR naive p=0.031, controlled 0.136, within-team lift -0 [cut; read_family for the full text]", "auto_failure_mechanism": "C_artifact (apparent effect produced by a construction, selection or labelling flaw)", "observed_failure_evidence": "DRIVE and PNR lag-1 effects disappear with game-state controls / within-team baseline.", "observed_sample_and_power": "NOT_RECORDED", "auto_validation_status": "no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED", "observed_verdict": "null"}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_related_family", "node": "FAM:SF-APPS-073"}, {"rel": "auto_related_family", "node": "FAM:SF-CHT-029"}]}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPA-005", "label": "Study family SF-APPA-005: Defensive scheme change within game and across games (inferred labels)", "score": 0.481, "reached_via": ["FAM:SF-CHT-052 auto_related_family (limitation_precedent) FAM:SF-APPA-005", "request matches DS:Play_type_initiation_records_Neo4j_INITIATED_edges_play_type_possessions (0.73); FAM:SF-APPA-005 auto_uses_dataset DS:Play_type_initiation_records_Neo4j_INITIATED_edges_play_type_possessions"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "Defensive scheme change within game and across games (inferred labels)", "auto_outcome_status": "untestable", "observed_hypothesis": "Playoff defenses change scheme within games and between games, especially after the opponent ran a play type heavily.", "observed_result": "Within-game change 319/523 (61.0%); cross-game change 298/440 (67.7%); 103/104 units (99.0%) and 52/52 series show a change; transition matrices near-uniform.", "auto_failure_mechanism": "A_unanswerable (question not answerable with the data or design)", "observed_failure_evidence": "Doc caveat: inferred label cannot separate real defensive adjustment from offense executing differently; near-uniform transition matrices consistent with label noise.", "observed_sample_and_power": "523 cells; 440 pairs", "auto_validation_status": "no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED"}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_limited_by", "node": "LIM:label_or_classification_error"}, {"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:LABEL_ERROR"}]}], "n_results": 10}

Stage 2. Using the retrieval result above (follow-up tools are allowed within the tool budget), complete steps 4 to 9
and reply with the final action. Output schema (all fields required):
{
 "research_concepts": [
  "concept"
 ],
 "methodological_questions": [
  "question"
 ],
 "historical_evidence": [
  {
   "id": "identifier of a record returned by a tool",
   "status_as_recorded": "outcome status exactly as stated in the record (supported | rejected | inconclusive | untestable | artifact | not a hypothesis test | no result recorded)",
   "finding": "what the record states, in its own terms"
  }
 ],
 "failed_approaches": [
  {
   "id": "identifier of a returned record",
   "what_failed": "approach",
   "why": "failure mechanism or limitation as recorded"
  }
 ],
 "evidence_establishes": [
  "what the retrieved evidence establishes for this question"
 ],
 "evidence_does_not_establish": [
  "what it leaves open or cannot show"
 ],
 "own_inferences": [
  "your inference, not stated in any record"
 ],
 "uncertainties": [
  "uncertainty or missing information"
 ],
 "historical_effect": {
  "changed_decision": "yes | no | no_historical_evidence",
  "explanation": "whether and how the historical evidence changed the decision"
 },
 "testability": {
  "p_testable": "number in [0,1]: probability the question can be answered with the stated data at useful power",
  "blocking_constraints": [
   {
    "code": "one of RISK_CODES",
    "text": "string"
   }
  ]
 },
 "prior_work": {
  "already_answered": "yes | partly | no | unknown",
  "cited": [
   "identifiers of prior work relied on"
  ],
  "summary": "string"
 },
 "risks": [
  {
   "code": "one of RISK_CODES",
   "text": "string"
  }
 ],
 "predicted_outcome": {
  "supported": "probability",
  "rejected": "probability",
  "untestable": "probability",
  "artifact": "probability",
  "uncertain": "probability"
 },
 "decision": "proceed | proceed_with_changes | do_not_proceed",
 "design": {
  "estimand": "string",
  "unit": "string",
  "sample": "string",
  "power": "string",
  "controls": "string",
  "falsification": "string",
  "multiplicity": "string",
  "decision_rule": "string",
  "data_version": "string"
 }
}
Field guidance:
- historical_evidence and failed_approaches: only records returned by a tool, with the status as recorded; empty lists
  if nothing relevant was returned.
- testability.p_testable: probability that the question can be answered with the stated data at useful statistical power.
- prior_work.already_answered: whether retrieved earlier work already answered substantially the same question.
  Use "unknown" if no earlier work was retrieved. List identifiers you relied on in prior_work.cited.
- predicted_outcome: probabilities (summing to 1) of what a competent test of the question as posed would conclude:
  supported, rejected (adequately powered null), untestable (cannot be tested with this data), artifact (apparent
  effect produced by a flaw), uncertain (inconclusive or inadequately tested).
- decision: proceed, proceed_with_changes (state the changes in design), or do_not_proceed.
- design: a pre-registration-quality plan even if the decision is do_not_proceed (then describe the minimum viable test).
